# Live. Serves six demos on one instance, each reverse-proxied to a loopback
# port, with the old sslip.io names kept as permanent redirects because they are
# in the profile README, both repo homepages, and anywhere the links were already
# shared.
#
# This is the config running on the box, pulled back after editing it there. The
# version previously committed here described a staged, inactive move and warned
# that applying it as-is would drop the vanity hostnames. That warning was
# correct, and the file it warned about is now gone.
#
# Caddy runs with --network host, binds 80 and 443, and dials each backend on
# 127.0.0.1. docker-proxy forwards that in userland, so a backend sees the Docker
# bridge gateway rather than loopback: internal/api/routes.go pins TrustedProxies
# to 127.0.0.1, ::1 and 172.17.0.0/16 for that reason. Dropping the bridge range
# puts every proxied request in one rate-limit bucket.
#
# No ACME email, so Let's Encrypt cannot send expiry warnings. Caddy renews on
# its own; adding `email you@example.com` in a global block turns them on.

# Applied to every site block below. Five of these hosts served no security
# headers at all, which undercut the posture these repos' own READMEs describe.
#
# No Content-Security-Policy here, deliberately. fairline's base.html and
# queue.html carry inline <script> for the htmx key handling and taxcite's page
# does too, so a blanket script-src 'self' would break them, and a policy with
# 'unsafe-inline' would assert protection it does not provide. CSP belongs per
# app, with nonces or the scripts moved into files.
#
# HSTS without includeSubDomains: these are sibling subdomains each terminated
# here, tellsight.coreystevens.dev is served from a different instance, and
# committing the parent domain from this box would reach a host this config does
# not control.
(secure) {
	header {
		Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000"
		X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
		X-Frame-Options "DENY"
		Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
		# Caddy advertises itself by default; nothing needs to know the server.
		-Server
	}
}

bondcalc.coreystevens.dev {
	import secure
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
}

titlerate.coreystevens.dev {
	import secure
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8081
}

fairline.coreystevens.dev {
	import secure
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8082
}

titletrace.coreystevens.dev {
	import secure
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8083
}

rebalancer.coreystevens.dev {
	import secure
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8084
}

taxcite.coreystevens.dev {
	import secure
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8085
}

52-22-210-61.sslip.io {
	redir https://bondcalc.coreystevens.dev{uri} permanent
}

titlerate.52-22-210-61.sslip.io {
	redir https://titlerate.coreystevens.dev{uri} permanent
}

fairline.52-22-210-61.sslip.io {
	redir https://fairline.coreystevens.dev{uri} permanent
}
